WEBVTT


00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:01.700
Korean versus Japanese skincare,

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:02.901
which one is actually better?

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:06.501
Because choosing the wrong one is why your skin isn't improving.

00:00:06.502 --> 00:00:07.821
Here's the real difference.

00:00:07.822 --> 00:00:10.221
Korean skincare is all about hydration and treatment.

00:00:10.222 --> 00:00:11.821
Think glass skin and dewy glow.

00:00:11.822 --> 00:00:14.321
They focus on layering products to keep your skin hydrated

00:00:14.322 --> 00:00:16.941
and they're best for dry, dehydrated and dull skin.

00:00:16.942 --> 00:00:19.501
Meanwhile, Japanese skincare is more minimal.

00:00:19.502 --> 00:00:21.421
Think bright and soft mochi skin.

00:00:21.422 --> 00:00:23.901
There's fewer steps and they're more focused on skin barrier,

00:00:23.902 --> 00:00:26.381
best for sensitive, irritated and acne prone skin.

00:00:26.382 --> 00:00:28.581
The truth is that neither is better than the other.

00:00:28.582 --> 00:00:29.581
They just do different things.

00:00:29.582 --> 00:00:33.061
So stop copying trends and choose what your skin actually needs.

00:00:33.062 --> 00:00:34.701
Both can be hard to find in North America,

00:00:34.702 --> 00:00:36.992
but you can find it all here at kiyoko. Com.
